  'You can write Python — now learn to think like a computer scientist. Discover what a program really is, design algorithms with guess-and-check, tame complexity with abstraction and decomposition, master recursion, build Big-O intuition for efficiency, implement searching and sorting, and debug like a professional with tests and exceptions. Finishes with an applied project where you implement linear and binary search and measure how they scale. Structure informed by MIT OpenCourseWare''s introductory programming sequence (CC BY-NC-SA).',
  null, 'foundations', 4, true, 'technology',
